  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the 4th-5th Century Yereruyk Basilica in Shirak Province</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Built between the 4th and 5th centuries, the ancient basilica of Yereruyk is an exemplar of early Armenian church architecture and its ancient Syrian and Hellenistic architectural influences. This project involves the conservation of the church and the preservation of ancient khachkars (cross-stones) and other monumental stone sculptures at the site.</narrative>
  </description>
